Abstract\par
Dynamic languages such as JavaScript are more difficult to com-\par
pile than statically typed ones. Since no concrete type information\par
is available, traditional compilers need to emit generic code that can\par
handle all possible type combinations at runtime. We present an al-\par
ternative compilation technique for dynamically-typed languages\par
that identifies frequently executed loop traces at run-time and then\par
generates machine code on the fly that is specialized for the ac-\par
tual dynamic types occurring on each path through the loop. Our\par
method provides cheap inter-procedural type specialization, and an\par
elegant and efficient way of incrementally compiling lazily discov-\par
ered alternative paths through nested loops. We have implemented\par
a dynamic compiler for JavaScript based on our technique and we\par
have measured speedups of 10x and more for certain benchmark\par
programs.\par
Categories and Subject DescriptorsD.3.4 [Programming Lan-\par
